"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a Phase 1 budget of $500,000 and a kick-off on June 15th. The project has established a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and the transition from the design phase to the development phase, led by Omar Jensen. The project is currently in phases involving idea gathering (R&D proposals due July 20th), feedback collection on the prototype (due end of November), and ongoing efforts to leverage AI for data visualization and cloud computing enhancements."
